completions_2:
Shannon eats 2 cookies a night and wants them to last 30 days. Therefore, she needs 2 cookies/night * 30 nights = 60 cookies.

Her recipe makes 1 dozen (12) cookies.   To find out how many dozens she needs, we divide the total number of cookies needed by the number of cookies per dozen:  60 cookies / 12 cookies/dozen = 5 dozens.

\boxed{5}

